  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The key to a proper lion head meatball is texture. The pork should be hand-chopped or coarsely minced, not fine. Chunks of fat in the mixture are desirable. This is "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "huaiyang-cuisine"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Huaiyang cuisine"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " at its most direct: good pork, simple seasoning, slow heat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "velveting-meatball"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "velveting"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " step using cornflour helps the meatballs hold together and keeps them tender. Do not overmix or pack the mixture tightly when shaping. Loose, rough meatballs are the goal."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
